{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"dae2de74fd840052","name":"card_unit_potez_63_11","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/units/card_unit_potez_63_11","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"POTEZ 63.11","text":"When you add or deploy a unit with Mobilize, draw a card and your HQ gains +2 defense.","flavorText":"The Potez 63.11 was a variant of the Potez 630 aircraft, a heavy fighter developed for the French Air Force in the 1930s and used in WWII, both by the Vichy French Air Force and Free French Air Forces. The 63.11 was the most numerous variant, with 730 units being manufactured. The 63.11 didn’t have the same speed and maneuverability as previous variants which made it vulnerable in the air. It was designed with a light bomber capability and came with a small bomb bay which could carry 8 x 10kg bombs and 2 x 50kg bombs could be carried under the wings. It was armed with 3 x MAC 1934s under the nose and some had additional guns in the wing gondolas.","faction":"France","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_potez_63_11","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_potez_63_11_title","SourceString":"POTEZ 63.11","LocalizedString":"POTEZ 63.11"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_potez_63_11_text","SourceString":"When you add or deploy a unit with Mobilize, draw a card and your HQ gains +2 defense.","LocalizedString":"When you add or deploy a unit with Mobilize, draw a card and your HQ gains +2 defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_potez_63_11_history","SourceString":"The Potez 63.11 was a variant of the Potez 630 aircraft, a heavy fighter developed for the French Air Force in the 1930s and used in WWII, both by the Vichy French Air Force and Free French Air Forces. The 63.11 was the most numerous variant, with 730 units being manufactured. The 63.11 didn’t have the same speed and maneuverability as previous variants which made it vulnerable in the air. It was designed with a light bomber capability and came with a small bomb bay which could carry 8 x 10kg bombs and 2 x 50kg bombs could be carried under the wings. It was armed with 3 x MAC 1934s under the nose and some had additional guns in the wing gondolas.","LocalizedString":"The Potez 63.11 was a variant of the Potez 630 aircraft, a heavy fighter developed for the French Air Force in the 1930s and used in WWII, both by the Vichy French Air Force and Free French Air Forces. The 63.11 was the most numerous variant, with 730 units being manufactured. The 63.11 didn’t have the same speed and maneuverability as previous variants which made it vulnerable in the air. It was designed with a light bomber capability and came with a small bomb bay which could carry 8 x 10kg bombs and 2 x 50kg bombs could be carried under the wings. It was armed with 3 x MAC 1934s under the nose and some had additional guns in the wing gondolas."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Mobilize"],"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/t_potez.t_potez","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Roy Grinnell","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/POTEZ_63_11.POTEZ_63_11","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":334.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_potez_63_11_photo","SourceString":"A Potez 63.11 in flight,